info={
'about':('About & editorial policy','How Deskwise Guide develops independent buying education for US and Japan readers.','''<p class="eyebrow">OUR APPROACH</p><h1>Make the decision clearer.</h1><p class="dek">Deskwise Guide is an independent editorial project about practical desks, phone accessories and everyday home-office technology for English-speaking readers in the US and Japan.</p><h2>What our guides do</h2><p>We turn common purchase decisions into useful checks: dimensions, compatibility, package contents, care, regional differences and reasons to buy nothing. Our examples illustrate a decision process rather than a universal best product.</p><h2>What our guides are based on</h2><p>Technical claims use linked manufacturer or standards-body references where relevant. Layout suggestions, comparison frameworks and illustrative scenarios are editorial guidance. We do not claim laboratory measurements, hands-on testing, customer interviews or ownership of products we have not tested.</p><h2>How this content is produced</h2><p>Deskwise uses AI assistance to draft and organize original educational content. This does not replace checking current manufacturer specifications. These launch guides are buying frameworks rather than tested-product rankings. Readers should verify the exact model and requirements before purchasing.</p><h2>Commercial independence</h2><p>No paid placements or sponsored rankings have been included in these launch guides. Current shopping links are non-affiliate links. Future commercial relationships will be disclosed close to the relevant links. We do not promise savings, availability, approval for an affiliate program or any particular purchase outcome.</p><h2>Corrections and updates</h2><p>Guides display their revision date. We revise content when a substantive error or changed specification is identified. Please include the guide URL and a reliable source when reporting a correction through our <a href="contact.html">contact page</a>.</p>'''),
'disclosure':('Affiliate disclosure','The current status of Deskwise Guide shopping links and how future affiliate links will be identified.','''<p class="eyebrow">TRANSPARENCY</p><h1>About our shopping links.</h1><p class="dek">Current status: no Amazon Associates tracking IDs are enabled. We earn no commission from the shopping links currently on this website.</p><h2>What the links open</h2><p>Our USA and Japan buttons open ordinary Amazon search pages. Results are controlled by the store and may include items we have not evaluated. A search link is not an endorsement of every result, seller or claim shown there.</p><h2>If affiliate links are introduced</h2><p>After the relevant Associates account is established, qualifying links may earn a commission. We will identify paid links close to the link, explain the relationship clearly and display the applicable required program disclosure. A US account or tracking ID will not be assumed to cover Japan.</p><h2>How we handle product information</h2><p>We do not copy Amazon customer reviews, display Amazon logos, invent discounts or publish live prices. The guides currently contain no product ratings or claims of firsthand tests. Product specifications and shopping conditions should be verified on the current manufacturer's and seller's pages.</p><h2>Independent publication</h2><p>Deskwise Guide is not owned, operated or endorsed by Amazon. Store names are used to identify shopping destinations. Our editorial aim is to make your buying decision more informed, including when that means keeping what you already own.</p>'''),
'contact':('Contact & corrections','Report a Deskwise Guide correction or ask a general editorial question through the project repository.','''<p class="eyebrow">GET IN TOUCH</p><h1>Help make the guides better.</h1><p class="dek">Use the Deskwise Guide project issue tracker for editorial questions, corrections and site problems.</p><a class="button" href="https://github.com/notorius69-cpu/deskwise-guide/issues/new" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Open a project issue ↗</a><h2>For a useful correction</h2><p>Include the guide URL, the sentence or feature concerned and a manufacturer or other primary reference if available. For a display problem, mention your browser and screen size. A GitHub account is required to post.</p><h2>Keep personal information private</h2><p>Project issues are public. Do not post addresses, phone numbers, order numbers, passwords, identity documents or other sensitive details. For account-specific privacy requests, use GitHub's available privacy and support routes rather than publishing personal data in an issue.</p><h2>Store orders and returns</h2><p>Deskwise does not sell or ship the products shown in linked stores. For an order, warranty, payment or return, contact the seller or marketplace directly. We cannot access your Amazon account.</p>'''),
'privacy':('Privacy notice','How this static Deskwise Guide site handles browsing, external links and public project issues.','''<p class="eyebrow">PRIVACY</p><h1>A simple site, with clear boundaries.</h1><p class="dek">Effective 2 November 2026. This notice describes the current static Deskwise Guide website.</p><h2>What this website includes</h2><p>The site has no visitor accounts, checkout, newsletter form, advertising scripts or analytics scripts. The guide filter runs in your browser and does not save your selection. Our own code does not set cookies or use browser storage.</p><h2>Hosting and technical information</h2><p>The website is published using OpenAI Sites and its Cloudflare-based hosting infrastructure. Hosting and security providers may process connection information such as IP address, request time, browser information and requested URL to deliver and protect the site. Deskwise does not specify a separate retention period for provider-controlled logs. Review <a href="https://openai.com/policies/privacy-policy/">OpenAI's privacy policy</a> and <a href="https://www.cloudflare.com/privacypolicy/">Cloudflare's privacy policy</a> for provider practices.</p><h2>Amazon and other outbound links</h2><p>Opening an external link takes you to another service with its own policies. Amazon shopping links currently contain no Associates tracking IDs. Amazon may process your visit under its own privacy and cookie practices. Deskwise does not receive your order, payment or account details from these ordinary links.</p><h2>Contact through GitHub</h2><p>Our contact route is the public GitHub project issue tracker. GitHub processes account information and posted content under <a href="https://docs.github.com/en/site-policy/privacy-policies/github-general-privacy-statement">its privacy statement</a>. Public issues are visible to others. Avoid posting personal or sensitive information.</p><h2>Questions and changes</h2><p>For a general website privacy question, use the <a href="contact.html">contact route</a> without posting sensitive details. If analytics, forms, accounts or affiliate tools are added, this notice must be updated to describe the resulting practices. The effective date above will change when the notice is revised.</p>''')}
